  "hybrid_definition": {
    "id": "C5_PEAK_ROOT_HYBRID",
    "label": "POST_HOC_MECHANISTIC_PROBE",
    "hypothesis": "C2 is better at LOCATING stable tonal evidence; C3 is better at INTERPRETING harmonic stacks as fundamental evidence. C3 draws its evidence from raw max-in-window spectral energy, which retains broadband and mainlobe-leakage contamination - J3G's diagnosis showed C3 salience accumulating on candidates at MIDI 59 and 61, which have no real partial, only the Hann mainlobe skirt of the 261.6 Hz fundamental. Feeding C3-style root inference from C2's interpolated peaks should remove exactly that contamination.",
    "single_variable_changed": "the EVIDENCE SOURCE for harmonic accumulation: interpolated spectral peaks instead of max-in-window bin energy. Everything else - candidate grid, harmonic count, harmonic weights, gate shape, gate constant, tolerance - is inherited unchanged from the corrected C3, so the comparison isolates the mechanism.",
    "formula": "Peaks: EXACTLY C2's peak set - local maxima of |X[k]| above the 40 Hz floor, parabolic interpolation on log-magnitude for sub-bin frequency and refined amplitude, kept when amplitude >= 0.01 of the frame's largest peak. Shared code, not a reimplementation. For candidate fundamental c on the equal-tempered semitone grid MIDI 28..96 and harmonic h = 1..8: A_h(c) = the amplitude of the LARGEST peak whose frequency lies within +/- 0.5 semitone of h*f0(c), or 0 if no peak lies there. S(c) = sum_h (1/h) * A_h(c). odd_support(c) = sum over odd h<=8 of (1/h)*A_h(c). odd_frac(c) = odd_support(c) / (S(c) + eta). Octave gate g(c) = min(1, odd_frac(c)/rho). Final salience S*(c) = S(c) * g(c). Fold: pitch_class[b] = sum over candidates c with (midi(c) mod 12 == b) of S*(c).",
    "declared_constants_frozen_before_any_corpus_evaluation": {
      "midi_low": 28,
      "midi_high": 96,
      "H": 8,
      "harmonic_weights": "1/h",
      "harmonic_match_half_width_semitones": 0.5,
      "rho": 0.767,
      "rho_derivation": "sum_{h odd <= 8} 1/h^2 / sum_{h <= 8} 1/h^2 = 1.1716 / 1.5274 - the odd-harmonic fraction of an ideal 1/h series under 1/h weights. Analytic, not fitted.",
      "eta": 1e-12,
      "peak_amplitude_threshold_relative": 0.01,
      "freq_floor_hz": 40.0,
      "tuning": "A440 fixed - J3G measured 0.68 cents median deviation on this corpus and recorded TUNING_NOT_MATERIAL_HERE",
      "native_domain": "amplitude",
      "carry_forward_compression": "P0_CURRENT, as determined by the J3G-1 ablation. For an amplitude-domain candidate that is exponent 1.0, i.e. the identity - the same treatment C3 received."
    },
    "guard_is_derived_from_peak_evidence_not_raw_windows": "the gate uses A_h(c) computed from PEAKS. This is the substantive difference from C3's guard: a sub-octave candidate's odd harmonics (1.5*f0, 2.5*f0) contain no local maximum at all, so the peak-based odd fraction collapses to near zero, whereas the raw-window version always found some leakage energy there.",
    "does_not_inherit_the_defective_formula": "the withdrawn original C3 form S*(c) = S(c) * odd_frac(c) is algebraically identical to odd_sum(c) and silently discards every even harmonic. The hybrid uses the SATURATING gate min(1, odd_frac/rho), so a clean fundamental keeps its full harmonic sum.",
    "no_zoo_no_sweep": "one hybrid, one constant set, frozen here. If it fails, the answer is the outcome below, not a C6."
  },
